{"path":"types/type_identity","title":"std::type_identity","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>type_identity","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/type_identity","section":"types","kind":"page","summary":"Provides the member typedef type that names T (i.e., the identity transformation).","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/type_traits\">&lt;type_traits&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> type_identity<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Provides the member typedef <code>type</code> that names <code>T</code> (i.e., the identity transformation).\n</p><p>If the program adds specializations for <code>std::type_identity</code>, the behavior is undefined.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Member_types\">Member types</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Name\n</td>\n<td> Definition\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>type</code>\n</td>\n<td> <code>T</code>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Helper_types\">Helper types</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">using</span> type_identity_t <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> type_identity<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">type</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3 id=\"Possible_implementation\">Possible implementation</h3>\n<table class=\"eq-fun-cpp-table\">\n<tr>\n<td>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> type_identity <span class=\"br0\">{</span> <span class=\"kw1\">using</span> type <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> T<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></code></pre>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes </h3>\n<p><code>std::type_identity</code> can be used to establish <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/template_argument_deduction#Non-deduced_contexts\">non-deduced contexts</a> in template argument deduction.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr></th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr></th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_type_identity\"><code>__cpp_lib_type_identity</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/20#cpp_lib_type_identity_201806L\"><code>201806L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++20)</span></td>\n<td><code>std::type_identity</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;type_traits&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\nT foo<span class=\"br0\">(</span>T a, T b<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span> <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> a <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> b<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\nT bar<span class=\"br0\">(</span>T a, std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">type_identity_t</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> b<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span> <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> a <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> b<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// foo(4.2, 1); // error, deduced conflicting types for 'T'</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> bar<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">4.2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>  <span class=\"co1\">// OK, calls bar&lt;double&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>5.2</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/identity\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>identity</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  function object that returns its argument unchanged <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member types","id":"Member_types"},{"depth":3,"text":"Helper types","id":"Helper_types"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"types","title":"Type support (basic types, RTTI)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::type_identity","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. Provides the member typedef type that names T (i.e., the identity transformation)."},{"label":"Member types","children":[{"label":"type","note":"T"}]},{"label":"Helper types"},{"label":"Possible implementation"},{"label":"Notes","note":"std::type_identity can be used to establish non-deduced contexts in template argument deduction."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"identity","note":"function object that returns its argument unchanged"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":153,"codeBlockCount":3}
